As global supply chains grow, warehouses require intelligent, scalable systems to handle dynamic logistics challenges. Traditional methods fail to deliver real-time adaptability and efficiency. 
This research introduces a novel integration of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) with Large Language Models (LLMs) to enable autonomous, context-aware warehouse decision-making. 
By combining robotics with advanced NLP, the system intelligently interprets orders, retrieves actionable insights, and executes tasks with minimal human input. The proposed framework demonstrates significant improvements in operational speed, accuracy, and scalability—especially within dark store environments.
